    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n73144" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀλίσθ-ημα</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ατος</span>,
			τό, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>slip, fall,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑγρὰ -ήματα ὑδάτων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Ti.</u>
					43c
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀ. γῆς</span>”
				<i>place where a landslip has occurred,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					J.
					<u>AJ</u>
					15.10.3
				</span></i>
			 ; so <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀ.</span> without <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γῆς,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				<u>Inscr.Prien.</u>
				42.10
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				42
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(ii B. C.)</span> ; in moral sense, <i>cause of slipping,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.49c
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>luxation,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Fract.</u>
				14
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Heliod.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Orib.
				49.9.16
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				19.460
			</span></i>, etc.</div>
